PE 835: Supernatural Numbers / 超自然数

=== Problem Statement ===
Supernatural numbers (Steinitz numbers) are formal products
∏ p^{v_p} where each v_p ∈ ℕ₀ ∪ {∞}.
Count/sum supernatural numbers with finite product bound N.

=== Supernatural Numbers Definition ===
A supernatural number is S = 2^{v_2} · 3^{v_3} · 5^{v_5} · ...
where v_p ∈ {0, 1, 2, ..., ∞}.
- If all v_p are finite: S is an ordinary natural number
- If any v_p = ∞: S is a 'truly' supernatural number

=== Counting supernatural numbers (finite part ≤ N) ===
For each natural n (finite part), primes not dividing n
can independently be 0 (absent) or ∞ (infinite).
Total = Σ_{n=1}^{N} 2^{π(N) - ω(n)}

